{"scenario": "seam/the-backend-may-call-only-what-the-front-serves", "requires": ["v1", "fake-backend"], "doc": "The seam rule (call 2): the backend's own connection (its peer pid) is not-allowed a method the backend serves, and subscribe (it hears the front through notifications); a call can never wait on the backend that made it. The vehicle is env/set, the method the backend still serves; its entry file is rewritten between the two calls."}
{"do": "root"}
{"do": "write_file", "path": "$ROOT/answers/env.json", "json": {"call_front": {"method": "env/set", "params": {"env": []}}, "then": {"result": {"applied": []}}}}
{"do": "start", "hub": "h", "env": {"DRGNX_FAKE_BACKEND_SCRIPT": "{\"env/set\": {\"from_file\": \"$ROOT/answers/env.json\"}}"}}
{"do": "connect", "conn": "c", "hub": "h"}
{"do": "send", "conn": "c", "json": {"id": 1, "method": "env/set", "params": {"env": []}}}
{"do": "expect", "conn": "c", "json": {"id": 1, "result": {"applied": []}}}
{"do": "backend_log", "expect_line": "the backend may call only what the front serves"}
{"do": "write_file", "path": "$ROOT/answers/env.json", "json": {"call_front": {"method": "subscribe"}, "then": {"result": {"applied": []}}}}
{"do": "send", "conn": "c", "json": {"id": 2, "method": "env/set", "params": {"env": []}}}
{"do": "expect", "conn": "c", "json": {"id": 2, "result": {"applied": []}}}
{"do": "backend_log", "expect_line": "the backend hears the front through notifications"}
{"do": "backend_log", "count": "\"method\":\"env/set\"", "at_least": 2, "at_most": 2, "for_ms": 300}
